, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Basorelief+Drum+Prin+C%C3%AEmpie&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2024 Smiling C"]}, {"t": 6367, "time": "01:46:07", "artist": "Wings", "title": "Silly Love Songs", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Wings+Silly+Love+Songs", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Wings+Silly+Love+Songs", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Wings+Silly+Love+Songs", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Wings+Silly+Love+Songs", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Wings+Silly+Love+Songs", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Wings+Silly+Love+Songs", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Wings+Silly+Love+Songs&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“A few songs back, we had Wings, their demo of Silly Love Songs from 1976.”", "A 1976 demo of 'Silly Love Songs' exists on the 2014 deluxe reissue of 'Wings at the Speed of Sound'."]}, {"t": 6690, "time": "01:51:30", "artist": "Spike Walters", "title": "Apollo 3", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Spike+Walters+Apollo+3", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Spike+Walters+Apollo+3", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Spike+Walters+Apollo+3", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Spike+Walters+Apollo+3", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Spike+Walters+Apollo+3", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Spike+Walters+Apollo+3", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Spike+Walters+Apollo+3&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“the song we heard before was by Spike Walters from the Netherlands, released in 1983. named Apollo 3”", "Dutch home-recording artist who self-released lo-fi synth/drum-machine LPs on his own Spike Records label in the early 1980s, matching the era and country — exact track 'Apollo 3' not independently confirmed."]}, {"t": 6726, "time": "01:52:06", "artist": "Grateful Dead", "title": "Here Comes Sunshine", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Grateful+Dead+Here+Comes+Sunshine", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Grateful+Dead+Here+Comes+Sunshine", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Grateful+Dead+Here+Comes+Sunshine", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Grateful+Dead+Here+Comes+Sunshine", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Grateful+Dead+Here+Comes+Sunshine", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Grateful+Dead+Here+Comes+Sunshine", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Grateful+Dead+Here+Comes+Sunshine&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“Right now we're listening to The Grateful Dead, Here Comes the Sunshine. That was remastered in 2013.”", "Track from 'Wake of the Flood' (1973), included in a 2013 remaster of the band's studio albums."]}, {"t": 6784, "time": "01:53:04", "artist": "Boom Catz", "title": "Sun Cat", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Boom+Catz+Sun+Cat", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Boom+Catz+Sun+Cat", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Boom+Catz+Sun+Cat", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Boom+Catz+Sun+Cat", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1773197174", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Boom+Catz+Sun+Cat", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Boom+Catz+Sun+Cat&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2024 BIGBAND"]}], "counts": {"high": 1, "mid": 9, "low": 8}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:03:42", "end": "00:05:05", "text": "Good evening. Sam here, producer of M5 on hosting duties tonight, which I'm quite excited about. It's been, I think, a month between shows. So thank you for Lilly for having me on. Firstly, I'd like to acknowledge the Gadigal people of the Eora Nation on which FBi broadcast on this evening. I'd like to extend that respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Not too sure what's in store for tonight. I'm excited. I think we'll be hearing a lot of this new agey ambient. This is Joanna Brook now with The Space Between, released in 1981. Re-released by an American label, the Numeria Group, in 2019. I think I'm going to keep it quite chill. I think everyone's had a nice big week. I know I have. So I wouldn't be surprised if we don't hear any percussion. There'll be some vocals, but lots of warm tones like what we're hearing now. Excited to hear from you all. If you want to text in 0435 123 945."}, {"start": "00:32:55", "end": "00:33:44", "text": "What we just listened to before was an artist named Jimmer Nicholson. I can't say too much, know too much about him. But what we're listening to now is Ambient Meditations by Hirumi Hasano, the founder of Yellow Magic Orchestra, alongside Ryuichi Sakamoto and Yukihiro Takahashi. This release is a solo release that he did in the 90s. I think it was 97. He's got such range. Some of his earlier albums in the 80s was really early, early experimental techno. We've got the ambience, we've got the disco, we've got it all."}, {"start": "00:49:54", "end": "00:50:33", "text": "I did say there was going to be no percussion, but I think I had to break my rule for Possum here. This is released on Mad Habitat Recordings, a Sydney label, in 2023. Possum is a group made up of Jackson Fester and a few others. incredible stuff says here on Mad Habitat's band camp it's recorded over the years of 2021 in Begola Hills"}, {"start": "01:37:23", "end": "01:37:56", "text": "Just thought I'd check in. I've got about four, twenty minutes to go, pardon me. At the moment we are listening to Yoshinori Sanohara, Earthbeat, on his album Lovebeat, released in 2001. Again, feel free to text in, love to know your thoughts, keep me some company, on 0435 123 945. I'll leave you with Yoshinori. Thank you."}, {"start": "01:52:42", "end": "01:53:33", "text": "Lots of cheap-sounding drum machines recently. A few songs back, we had Wings, their demo of Silly Love Songs from 1976. Right now we're listening to The Grateful Dead, Here Comes the Sunshine. That was remastered in 2013. This is another demo. And the song we heard before was by Spike Walters from the Netherlands, released in 1983. named Apollo 3 this will be it for me I think there's a couple more songs to go and then it is time for the all night crew it's been good to host thank you very much and again thank you to Lily for having me I hope everyone has enjoyed"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "-1:59:50"}, "track": {"title": "The Space Between", "artists": [{"name": "Joanna Brouk"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:32:08"}, "track": {"title": null, "artists": [{"name": "Jimmer Nicholson"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:32:31"}, "track": {"title": "Ambient Meditations", "artists": [{"name": "Haruomi Hosono"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:35:00"}, "track": {"title": "S